WEBVTT

00:18.351 --> 00:22.147
She did all of this on her own...

00:29.821 --> 00:31.239
Senku!

00:31.823 --> 00:33.158
Over there!

00:36.036 --> 00:38.788
NITRIC ACID FIELD

00:43.293 --> 00:44.669
It took me

00:46.129 --> 00:50.842
<i>so, so many years to get here...</i>

00:52.802 --> 00:57.640
<i>I failed so, so many times...</i>

01:01.227 --> 01:04.731
A saltpeter field made from animal waste...

01:05.690 --> 01:09.486
The method was commonly used in Japan
during the Sengoku era.

01:10.028 --> 01:12.238
It takes a ridiculous amount of time...

01:13.323 --> 01:14.491
<i>In spite of that,</i>

01:14.574 --> 01:21.247
<i>it's a ten billion percent certain
and steady way to get the Revival Fluid.</i>

01:22.832 --> 01:24.209
You truly are something...

01:25.001 --> 01:26.211
Suika.

01:29.297 --> 01:32.008
But I could only make enough
for one person,

01:32.091 --> 01:34.677
so I decided to wake you up first.

01:35.762 --> 01:39.724
Yeah, the order's correct too.
You get a full ten billion points.

01:40.600 --> 01:44.896
Well, it's time for a science craft show
seven years worth of work.

01:47.524 --> 01:49.109
ORIGINAL WORK: RIICHIRO INAGAKI, BOICHI
SHUEISHA "JUMP COMICS"

03:33.755 --> 03:36.174
- Done.
- In just a day?

03:36.257 --> 03:38.676
But it took me so many years!

03:38.760 --> 03:41.137
I knew you'd be so amazing, Senku!

03:41.221 --> 03:42.180
‎OBTAINED NITRIC ACID!

03:42.263 --> 03:44.641
I just made it in a different way.

03:44.724 --> 03:47.727
It's super quick
if you have some platinum.

03:51.105 --> 03:53.733
<i>Then we just need alcohol.</i>

03:53.816 --> 03:56.819
We'll need to wait half a month
until it ferments.

03:57.737 --> 04:02.867
Meanwhile, we'll have to make
more nitric acid every day.

04:04.285 --> 04:07.121
In 16 days,
we'll have 16 vials of Revival Fluid.

04:07.205 --> 04:09.415
All done in one go.

04:35.858 --> 04:37.277
Suika?

04:41.489 --> 04:46.953
Looks like we're more or less
the same age now, Kohaku...

04:47.704 --> 04:52.625
I guess I can't ask you for hugs anymore...

05:22.530 --> 05:24.115
Ryusui! François!

05:24.198 --> 05:27.201
It's been a long time, Miss Suika.

05:28.995 --> 05:31.706
You really gave it all, Suika.

05:35.626 --> 05:37.670
There are 16 vials of Revival Fluid.

05:38.421 --> 05:41.799
That means there's enough for all of us.

05:44.010 --> 05:46.804
We'll discuss what to do
about the enemies tomorrow.

05:46.888 --> 05:50.433
For now,
let's just bring all our allies back!

06:07.200 --> 06:11.704
As always, I feel amazing
once I come out of petrification!

06:11.788 --> 06:13.623
I wonder if someone as old as me

06:13.706 --> 06:16.459
could still make it
to the end of our adventure

06:16.542 --> 06:18.628
if I got petrified now and then.

06:19.212 --> 06:21.631
Besides, it looks like Suika's grown up.

06:21.714 --> 06:25.760
Aren't you all catching up to my age too?

06:27.178 --> 06:29.263
Wait...

06:29.347 --> 06:34.268
Could we have kept Kaseki as a stone
for a while to let him live longer?

06:34.352 --> 06:39.315
There's no way the petrification device
could bring him back if he dies, right?

06:40.024 --> 06:40.942
Oh, no!

06:41.025 --> 06:43.694
We couldn't possibly fix
the ships and all without you, Kaseki.

06:45.029 --> 06:48.241
You really are relying on me!
I'll do my best!

06:48.324 --> 06:49.325
- Senku.
- Huh?

06:51.744 --> 06:52.787
What about Hyoga?

06:55.373 --> 06:58.793
Yeah, we're using our last vial
of Revival Fluid on him.

07:00.253 --> 07:03.881
And then our group of friends
will be complete!

07:03.965 --> 07:07.218
I've been waiting years for this
after putting you all in line.

07:09.303 --> 07:12.056
There's a chance that Hyoga won't...

07:36.706 --> 07:39.125
- Whoa!
- Whoa!

07:39.208 --> 07:43.212
There's always that perfect line
to drop at a time like this, Hyoga!

07:43.296 --> 07:46.674
Do you mean "thank you"?
You really don't have to.

07:46.757 --> 07:49.385
That's not it. I'm talking about Hyoga's...

07:53.097 --> 07:56.392
Really on point, indeed.

07:57.810 --> 07:59.979
You're all the best!

08:10.031 --> 08:12.617
- Hurrah!
- Hurrah!

08:21.417 --> 08:23.252
Starting tomorrow,

08:23.336 --> 08:26.297
we'll be reviving everyone
in North America, Japan, Treasure Island...

08:26.881 --> 08:31.928
No, we'll be reviving
every human on earth once again!

08:32.803 --> 08:36.474
But tonight, we're having a victory feast!

08:45.816 --> 08:49.111
What's wrong, Suika? You're not eating...

08:50.112 --> 08:53.991
Every day, I always ate my meals alone.

08:55.159 --> 08:58.746
<i>Always... All alone...</i>

09:01.332 --> 09:07.213
That's why I somehow feel full already

09:07.797 --> 09:10.967
just by being with everyone!

09:12.134 --> 09:13.594
Suika...

09:16.180 --> 09:18.516
We're supposed to have a party tonight!

09:18.599 --> 09:21.477
Just being happy with
filling your heart's hunger

09:21.561 --> 09:24.230
is way too humble, don't you think?

09:24.897 --> 09:25.898
Here it is.

09:26.482 --> 09:28.693
If you want it, there you go.

09:30.403 --> 09:33.197
It's coconut milk fruit soup.

09:52.717 --> 09:54.594
It's delicious!

09:55.553 --> 10:01.475
It tastes even better
because I'm eating with all of you!

10:03.019 --> 10:08.190
This is the tastiest stuff
I've ever had in my life!

10:27.293 --> 10:31.505
By the way, Senku,
you kept your cracks from the revival.

10:32.590 --> 10:36.344
In the end, the cracks just
weathered away as they were.

10:37.219 --> 10:38.095
Senku...

10:40.306 --> 10:44.435
It looks like Tsukasa
went to the watermill by himself...

10:51.942 --> 10:52.943
Senku?

10:53.527 --> 10:56.364
I need everyone's attention!

10:56.447 --> 10:59.367
The mentalist is back after seven years!

10:59.450 --> 11:02.453
And I'll give you a victory magic show!

11:06.082 --> 11:08.626
- Yeah!
- Hooray!

11:18.052 --> 11:20.930
Damn... I drank too much!

11:27.645 --> 11:31.399
<i>Could we have kept Kaseki
as a stone for a while</i>

11:31.482 --> 11:33.067
<i>to let him live longer?</i>

11:35.653 --> 11:37.571
<i>Oh, well...</i>

11:38.948 --> 11:43.536
Out of all of us that got depetrified,

11:43.619 --> 11:46.122
Kaseki will be the first to go.

11:47.206 --> 11:50.960
I had never thought about that before.

11:58.509 --> 12:00.469
Since he had lost consciousness,

12:01.011 --> 12:03.931
Hyoga couldn't have noticed himself,

12:05.391 --> 12:09.395
<i>but he was already dead by then.</i>

12:11.981 --> 12:14.275
I had plenty of time.

12:14.984 --> 12:16.402
I didn't get it wrong.

12:18.362 --> 12:22.450
If it's coming from you, Tsukasa,
then it can't be wrong.

12:23.242 --> 12:27.288
I've had this hypothesis
ever since my neck was broken,

12:27.371 --> 12:29.874
or since you were in your cold sleep.

12:30.583 --> 12:33.127
And I had been able to prove it

12:33.210 --> 12:36.297
through an unintentional,
life-risking experiment.

12:38.757 --> 12:41.552
<i>Petrification rejects even death itself.</i>

12:43.053 --> 12:45.347
<i>Whyman's Dr. Stone...</i>

12:47.475 --> 12:49.602
<i>is a scientific taboo</i>

12:49.685 --> 12:53.147
<i>about resurrecting the dead
that humans shouldn't touch.</i>

12:53.230 --> 12:55.024
<i>A forbidden fruit.</i>

12:57.067 --> 13:01.197
In other words,
at this very moment, we hold

13:02.114 --> 13:04.200
the key to eternal life...

13:08.829 --> 13:11.832
for every human on Earth.

13:19.340 --> 13:22.259
Awesome!

13:23.219 --> 13:26.514
Are you serious? This is awesome!
In that case...

13:29.183 --> 13:31.018
Kaseki will keep on living too!

13:31.101 --> 13:35.606
Yeah, that could be possible.
We should thank Whyman.

13:35.689 --> 13:38.943
He was just acting like a villain
because he was scary.

13:39.026 --> 13:41.487
Maybe he's actually a really good guy?

13:42.196 --> 13:45.950
But he's trying to turn us all into stone...

13:46.575 --> 13:50.454
I don't get it.
What kind of guy is Whyman?

13:50.538 --> 13:52.414
Our only option

13:53.249 --> 13:57.419
is to go ask him
before Medusa rains down on Earth again.

13:57.503 --> 13:58.462
‎Yeah.

13:59.421 --> 14:01.507
<i>All the way to the Moon.</i>

14:02.758 --> 14:05.970
We're actually planning
a fun trip to the Moon?

14:06.053 --> 14:11.809
Whoa! How convenient
that you have a hardcore expert here!

14:12.643 --> 14:15.646
Freshly made Revival Fluid,
vial number 17.

14:15.729 --> 14:18.941
Is it really alright
to revive Xeno already?

14:22.570 --> 14:23.988
It's fine.

14:24.530 --> 14:26.031
That's right...

14:26.115 --> 14:29.326
As long as you're here, Tsukasa,
he can't go on a rampage or anything.

14:29.410 --> 14:31.328
As long as we can keep Stanley
under control.

14:33.205 --> 14:37.293
It might not even be a problem
of brute force anymore.

14:38.127 --> 14:43.382
That thing has changed the rules
of this world, ten billion percent.

14:49.597 --> 14:51.223
<i>The light of immortality!</i>

14:53.017 --> 14:58.105
It's an elegant yet wicked science
that defies the laws of nature.

14:58.188 --> 15:02.651
Wicked? Do you mean it's bad?
Why is it bad?

15:03.235 --> 15:05.404
Starting now, no one will ever die again!

15:05.487 --> 15:08.198
Isn't this the most amazing science ever?

15:09.575 --> 15:11.076
I'll tell everyone...

15:12.036 --> 15:15.080
Never dying is the same as dying.

15:15.831 --> 15:18.542
It can be even more terrifying.

15:21.378 --> 15:23.297
<i>A never ending world.</i>

15:24.423 --> 15:27.509
<i>Millions, trillions of old people</i>

15:28.177 --> 15:32.556
<i>would crowd our little planet.</i>

15:33.724 --> 15:35.643
<i>Food and resources would be limited.</i>

15:36.518 --> 15:39.355
<i>It would inevitably become a realm</i>

15:39.980 --> 15:46.946
<i>where a self-proclaimed God decides
who to purge by eternal petrification.</i>

15:47.780 --> 15:49.114
<i>A dystopia!</i>

15:52.785 --> 15:57.915
Whether we can fight cellular aging
will forever remain a mystery.

15:57.998 --> 16:00.000
The device is out of battery.

16:00.084 --> 16:02.711
There's no way
to conduct clinical trials now.

16:04.171 --> 16:06.382
Until we figure out the details,

16:06.465 --> 16:09.468
it's better if we keep this
between the four of us.

16:12.471 --> 16:14.640
<i>If the future revived ones</i>

16:14.723 --> 16:17.393
<i>hear about the possibility
of a world without death,</i>

16:17.476 --> 16:19.645
<i>the rules of the world
could change drastically.</i>

16:20.479 --> 16:22.815
<i>It could get out of control.</i>

16:25.234 --> 16:29.113
Dr. Stone, that controls eternal life.

16:30.030 --> 16:35.285
If we get control of this science,
we could become absolute dictators.

16:35.995 --> 16:38.914
But you still took the risk
and showed it to me.

16:39.707 --> 16:41.542
What was the reason?

16:43.627 --> 16:44.712
That...

16:45.504 --> 16:46.797
Isn't that the intercom

16:47.381 --> 16:49.967
that picks up sounds over radio waves,
from Treasure Island?

16:50.592 --> 16:57.558
Whyman's example of
"12,800,000 meters, one second."

16:58.642 --> 17:02.771
The frequency is set
so you can hear the lunar broadcast.

17:05.774 --> 17:07.860
It's in complete silence.

17:08.444 --> 17:12.281
The petrification voice
that Whyman kept blasting...

17:12.364 --> 17:16.910
As soon as the humans stopped moving,
he hasn't said a word.

17:16.994 --> 17:19.538
Isn't it obvious?

17:19.621 --> 17:23.250
Xeno, I don't know the reasons,
but Whyman...

17:24.084 --> 17:29.631
<i>is trying to turn everyone to stone
as long as humans exist in this world.</i>

17:30.132 --> 17:34.595
The rules for humans have
completely changed in this New World.

17:36.263 --> 17:39.433
There are no more dictatorships
or anything like that.

17:42.978 --> 17:45.814
And everyone is immortal.

17:46.607 --> 17:51.945
<i>In exchange, we're forever trapped
in Whyman's stone prison.</i>

17:53.113 --> 17:55.491
If someone isn't happy with that...

17:58.243 --> 18:00.496
So we have no choice

18:00.579 --> 18:03.499
but to go to the Moon
and settle this directly, right?

18:14.843 --> 18:17.596
All of Stanley Snyder's attacks
were either:

18:17.679 --> 18:21.725
A: Legitimate acts of combat
on the battlefield.

18:21.809 --> 18:24.103
B: Murder attempts.

18:25.145 --> 18:28.273
It's us who get to testify here.
Am I right?

18:29.108 --> 18:32.611
If we bring back Stanley
after restoring civilization...

18:32.694 --> 18:36.156
We will all testify it was option A.

18:36.240 --> 18:38.659
This is a card we can give to Xeno.

18:48.085 --> 18:49.711
And in exchange for your card,

18:49.795 --> 18:54.633
you get Dr. Xeno from NASA's
full cooperation in building a rocket.

18:55.592 --> 18:57.886
What an elegant deal.

18:59.388 --> 19:02.391
Wouldn't it be risky
to bring Xeno's friends here?

19:03.308 --> 19:07.146
I don't think Xeno would betray us,
given the circumstances.

19:08.730 --> 19:13.527
Still, this ceremony is really important.

19:13.610 --> 19:17.781
Xeno will cooperate with the plan
for the sake of his pride, too.

19:18.365 --> 19:22.327
Hey, Gen... did you happen
to hear that yesterday too?

19:22.411 --> 19:24.538
Huh? What do you mean?

19:37.926 --> 19:39.386
I'll do it.

20:14.671 --> 20:17.466
Let's begin, then.

20:22.554 --> 20:25.140
DR. XENO JOINED YOUR GROUP!

20:39.321 --> 20:40.364
It took ten...

20:40.447 --> 20:44.326
no, 3,700 years,

20:44.409 --> 20:46.870
but we finally joined forces...

20:46.954 --> 20:50.123
To build a spaceship in a stone world.

20:51.917 --> 20:54.378
Having traveled thousands of kilometers
away from Japan...

20:59.091 --> 21:00.509
Now, at last,

21:00.592 --> 21:03.762
we're at the starting line
on our way to space!

21:05.389 --> 21:11.603
Through oceans and mountains,
and now across the vast skies too!

21:21.947 --> 21:26.702
If we keep going steadily,
step by step, we'll definitely get there!

21:28.370 --> 21:31.373
All right, time to start crafting!

21:31.456 --> 21:32.791
START
RARE METAL

21:32.874 --> 21:36.336
This is our roadmap to the spaceship!

21:36.420 --> 21:38.380
SPACESHIP
GOAL

21:52.269 --> 21:56.440
Our final step
for the revival of humanity.

21:56.523 --> 22:01.862
We'll take back the future
of 7.8 billion people

22:02.904 --> 22:04.698
from Whyman's hands!

22:11.496 --> 22:14.416
This is tempting!

23:53.098 --> 23:55.892
NEXT EPISODE

23:55.976 --> 23:57.769
THIS WORK OF FICTION FEATURES ORGANISMS,
MATERIAL AND PROCESSES BASED ON REAL LIFE.

23:57.853 --> 23:59.396
COLLECTING OR REPLICATING THEM
MAY BE DANGEROUS AND ILLEGAL,

23:59.479 --> 24:00.897
SO DO NOT ATTEMPT.

24:00.981 --> 24:01.940
Subtitle translation by: Silvia Tomey
